                <p>We require participants for studies. Our needs for each trial or study may vary.</p>
                <p>
                <ul>
                <li><a href="#">OPEN FOR ENROLLMENT: Clinical Trial of of A New Investigational Toothpaste</a></li>
    <li><a href="#">OPEN FOR ENROLLMENT: Pain Assessment in Patients with Oral Cancer</a></li>
     <li><a href="#">DENTISTS ONLY: We need participation in the STOHN Molar-Incisor Hypomineralization Study to examine children in South Texas. This helps us to learn how often Molar-Incisor Hypomineralization occurs in South Texas.</a></li></p>
     <h4>Why should I consider a clinical trial?</h4>
     <p>When you participate in a clinical trial, you help bring new techniques, tools and treatments to dental practices worldwide.</p>
     <h4>Is it safe?</h4>
     <p>All clinical studies must go through a rigorous approval process through the Institutional Review Board before they are opened to the public. A principal investigator, who is often a medical doctor or dentist, leads the study. A research team may include doctors, dentists, hygienists, nurses, social workers and other health care professionals.</p>
     <h4>How do I sign up?</h4>
     <p>See if there is an available clinical trial that fits your needs as a patient. Trials open for enrollment are updated regularly.</p>
